          "entradaId": "freeman-756",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "For a description of books, and the mode of opening and closing (referred to in this verse and in verse twenty) see notes on Job 19:23-24 (#414) and on Isaiah 34:4 (#511). Each of the prophetical books is supposed to have been in a separate volume, with the exception of the proph…"
      },
      "c-fc3652b0b56c9be2": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-755",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "When the law and the prophets were read in the synagogue those who read were expected to stand. See note on Acts 13:15 (#834). Not only priests and Levites but common Israelites were allowed to read the Scriptures publicly. Every Sabbath seven persons read: a priest, a Levite, an…"
      }
